         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_game",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Game\n\nTwo numbers appear: **A** on the left and **B** on the right. Ask yourself: is B greater than A? In other words, are the numbers in order (A < B)? (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).\n\nChoose **In order** when the right number is greater than the left one, or **Not in order** when it is smaller. The open side of the symbol always faces the larger number. This time the numbers may have one decimal position. There are four levels: the first compares only integers from 0 to 9; the second compares numbers with the same integer part but different decimals; the third compares numbers between 0 and 100, each with one decimal position, without needing the same integer part; and the last compares a small number between 0 and 9 with one between 1 million and 10 million, both with a decimal position, so we write much greater (≫) and much less (≪). The game explains each answer. To try another pair, click the **New exercise** button, and after a correct answer you can move to the **Next level**.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "c47a586f-6053-4b8e-8f9b-828cd6220110",
                     "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "4e3c3945-0bf4-4040-9735-546541b27a50",
                     "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
